-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
                 CODE FARMS C/C++ DATA OBJECT LIBRARY
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  (Winner of the Computer Language JOLT AWARD, best 1992 Language/Library)

The  diskette is organized into directories and files,  which you can   examine
using your favourite text editor. Each directory has a README file, which helps
you to find the right information.

At the root directory, you have the following options:

 BROCHURE - marketing brochures, which we normally distribute printed on paper;
 TUTORIAL - tutorial on the use of the library (reprinted from our Users Guide);
 QUESTION - frequently asked questions, and answers to them;
 BUSINESS - business/legal information, including forms to order the product;
 CLASSES  - list of available classes and functions;
 REFER    - references to papers published on related topics;
 EX*      - code examples in C 
 EXX*     - code examples in C++

If you don't know much about our library, start with BROCHURE and TUTORIAL.

Each example is in a separate directory,  and contains the program itself,  two
automatically generated files,  and the executable (compiled with Borland C++).
Comments throughout the code and the README file explain how each program works.
